%N A399647 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} H(2*k)/(k*(2*k+1)), where H(k) = A001008(k)/A002805(k) is the k-th harmonic number.
%D A399647 H. Bremekamp, Problem, Nieuw. Arch. Wisk. (Ser. 3), Vol. 5 (1957), p. 48.
%H A399647 M. G. Beumer, <a href="https://www.jstor.org/stable/2311513">Some Special Integrals</a>, The American Mathematical Monthly, Vol. 68, No. 7 (1961), pp. 645-647.
%H A399647 Michael I. Shamos, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20220206102634/https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.366.9997&amp;rep=rep1&amp;type=pdf">A catalog of the real numbers</a>, 2011. See p. 356.
%H A399647 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A399647 Equals Pi^2/12 + log(2)^2 = zeta(2)/2 + log(2)^2 = A072691 + A253191.
%F A399647 Equals -Integral_{x=0..1} log(x/2)/(1+x) dx (Shamos, 2011).
%F A399647 Equals (1/Pi) * Integral_{x=0..Pi} (log(sin(x)))^2 dx = Integral_{x=0..1} (log(sin(Pi*x)))^2 dx (Bremekamp, 1957; Beumer, 1961).
%F A399647 Equals 4 * A397229.
%e A399647 1.302920047342314642903310109649677566340027902197944...
%t A399647 RealDigits[Zeta[2]/2 + Log[2]^2, 10, 120][[1]]
%o A399647 (PARI) zeta(2)/2 + log(2)^2
%Y A399647 Cf. A001008, A002805.
%Y A399647 Cf. A072691, A253191 ((1/2)*Sum_{k>=1} H(k)/(k*(2k+1))), A397229.
%K A399647 nonn,cons,new
%O A399647 1,2
